Wait longer in the X11 events thread once neither input nor frames have come for half a second.

The loop waited 1 ms in select() on every pass, waking about a thousand times a second while the
app was idle. The wait now follows the last activity: 1 ms while events arrived or a frame was
swapped within the last 500 ms, and 100 ms after that. The renderer's buffer swaps (GLX and
Present) share the display connection and can read events off the socket into xcb's queue, where
select() cannot see them, so a drawing app keeps the short wait; swap_buffers() records the time
in last_frame_usec for the events thread. Before waiting, XEventsQueued with QueuedAfterFlush
moves what waits on the socket and in xcb's queue into Xlib's queue, and the wait is skipped
when an event is there.

Races left open: a main-thread round trip while nothing draws, more than 500 ms after the last
input, can read an event that the 100 ms select() then misses, so that event is handled up to
100 ms later. Pointer motion over other windows reaches the events thread through the root
window's raw motion events (XI_RawMotion), which keeps the 1 ms wait while the pointer moves
anywhere.

diff --git a/platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp b/platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp
index 6936b32..d427d91 100644
--- a/platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp
+++ b/platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp
@@ -4693,15 +4693,32 @@ bool DisplayServerX11::_wait_for_events(int timeout_seconds, int timeout_microse
 }
 
 void DisplayServerX11::_poll_events() {
+	// select() cannot see events another call on this connection already read off the socket into
+	// Xlib's or xcb's queue, such as a round trip or the renderer's buffer swap on the main thread.
+	// So the wait is short while input keeps coming or frames are drawn, and long once neither
+	// happened for half a second.
+	uint64_t last_event_usec = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();
 	while (!events_thread_done.is_set()) {
-		// Wait with a shorter timeout from the events thread to avoid delayed inputs.
-		_wait_for_events(0, 1000);
+		const uint64_t now = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();
+		const uint64_t last_activity = MAX(last_event_usec, last_frame_usec.get());
+		const bool idle = now > last_activity && now - last_activity > 500000;
+		// QueuedAfterFlush also moves what waits on the socket and in xcb's queue into Xlib's, so
+		// an event read before this check is handled without waiting.
+		if (XEventsQueued(x11_display, QueuedAfterFlush) == 0) {
+			_wait_for_events(0, idle ? 100000 : 1000);
+		}
 
 		// Process events from the queue.
+		bool got_events = false;
 		{
 			MutexLock mutex_lock(events_mutex);
 
+			const uint32_t before = polled_events.size();
 			_check_pending_events(polled_events);
+			got_events = polled_events.size() > before;
+		}
+		if (got_events) {
+			last_event_usec = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec();
 		}
 	}
 }
@@ -5765,6 +5782,7 @@ void DisplayServerX11::release_rendering_thread() {
 }
 
 void DisplayServerX11::swap_buffers() {
+	last_frame_usec.set(OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec());
 #if defined(GLES3_ENABLED)
 	if (gl_manager) {
 		gl_manager->swap_buffers();
